{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899766-closest-splat-to-a-bleach-quincy","id":899766,"title":"Closest splat to a Bleach Quincy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-25T22:39:26-07:00","id":899766,"title":"Closest splat to a Bleach Quincy?","content":"If I were to try and create a Quincy from Bleach, which splat would work best?<br /> <br /> Or, should I just homebrew a splat? Any advice for that?<br /> <br /> I was working on a Mage Legacy for them, but I've kind of stalled on that.... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T00:51:33-07:00","id":899834,"title":"","content":"What part of the Qunicy is appealing to you? The high action manga/anime stuff is pretty much off the table.<br /> <br /> If you just want, &quot;Can see Twilight entities, and fires arrows of spiritual energy,&quot; from early Bleach, that's pretty easy via mortals + supernatural Merits, Hunter, or Mage.<br /> <br /> Mid-range Bleach where you start seeing Quincy flash-steps, arsenals of mystic booster items, and mini-gun level arrow storms, we're getting into higher end Mage stuff.<br /> <br /> If we get into the Sternritter... we're pretty much beyond the CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T03:04:05-07:00","id":899892,"title":"","content":"I'd go for hunter, dark hero, or proximi family myself, they aren't versatile enough for mage as a rule, and if you want the power level of bleach use the scope rules from the superhero hack from the mage chroniclers guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T10:04:46-07:00","id":900149,"title":"","content":"It really depends on what point in the story we're talking about though. By the start of X-cution arc, Ishida had pulled out enough tricks that he's gotten into Mage territory to adequately represent it all without a massive list of Merits. The Sternritter invasion of the Soul Society arc shows that Qunicy are capable of at their highest levels... and yeah, their powers are diverse enough for Mage.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's possible that most Qunicy aren't full Mages and only those powerful enough to join the ranks of the Sternritter should be modeled as such, with the rest as Proximi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:29:09-07:00","id":900252,"title":"","content":"You should try with Exalted templates and their Charms instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:12:44-07:00","id":900288,"title":"","content":"I agree with StSword, hunter may be the best bet. I'd say a conspiracy like the lucifuge where it is a bloodline related conspiracy. Benedictions and castigations after all do come close to invoking the feeling of quincy powers. Since the quincy are still pretty much human I do feel that hunter would be the best focus. Hollows were all once ghosts so probably design the conspiracy to be able to see and deal with ghosts or even just beings in twilight. <br /> <br /> They have a limited focus and a specialized set of powers so I feel the quincy could be represented best as a hunter conspiracy.<br /> <br /> To push it further the shinigami of bleach are also comparable in their duties to sin eaters even though their actual power and being is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:02:26-07:00","id":900333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899766-closest-splat-to-a-bleach-quincy?p=900288#post900288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have a limited focus and a specialized set of powers...</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that this isn't true to Bleach canon.<br /> <br /> The Ishidas self-limited because they didn't want to get caught up in the Wandenreich and specifically Jhwach's plans.<br /> <br /> The full abilities of the Quincy are highly varied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:11:58-07:00","id":900342,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I'm only aware of the light bow as well as their ability to see ghosts and hollows. I know they can do more than just that but aren't their powers mostly focused on dealing with hollows? Compared the a MtAw mage though wouldn't the highly varied quincy still seem specialized? I think the quincy powers are closer to hunter endowments than a mage's arcana. I am doubtful they'd compare to werewolf gifts or vampire disciplines but I don't have enough knowledge on the source material to actually say that with any certainty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T15:03:40-07:00","id":900398,"title":"","content":"Their base powers focus on channeling ambient spiritual energy and expelling it. The choice to employ this as a weapon against Hollows is a philosophic one, not an inherent one. The Shinigami are the ones with the natural Hollow focused powers since they can cleanse souls. Quincy energy is antithetical to Hollow energy, and the Quincy opt to destroy Hollows to keep them from interfering with their own powers. Shinigami energy is parallel to Hollow energy, allowing the Shinigami to cleanse Hollows to maintain the flow of souls and why Shinigami can become Vizoreds.<br /> <br /> The Sternritter's Elite Guard are equivalent in power level to Shinigami Captains, if not more potent. In the current arc <b>one</b> of them is currently fighting three Captains at once and it's mostly a stalemate (which is extremely impressive when one of those three is Kenpachi with his bankai achieved).<br /> <br /> That was my point about people like Uryu being &quot;self limited.&quot; The Ishidas didn't want to engage in the efforts to evolve their powers because they didn't feel it was what Quincy should be doing. Jhwach disagreed. He and his followers (who are the majority of the currently living Quincy) have advanced what Quincies are capable of to extreme levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T15:44:46-07:00","id":900420,"title":"","content":"I thought Bleach was over, is it still going on? I remember the glasses kid being a Quincy but I didn't read too much past that, I think they were still in the ghost kingdom. It's been years.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's going to depend on how faithful and deep TheScottishFianna wants to go with it. A spirit-archer is going to be easy, the rest seems like it might be getting really complex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:13:39-07:00","id":900435,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking the Hunter idea works well, since Paradox isn't an issue, although the mechanical stuff escapes me, usually. <br /> <br /> As far as how far to take it, I was thinking Uryu around the invasion of Hueco Mundo, not Wandereich level.<br /> <br /> Also, Seele Schneider and such would be good items as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:28:04-07:00","id":900443,"title":"","content":"Just as a possible suggestion for mechanics for the quincy light bow it could be as simple as for a willpower you summon a bow of light that lasts for the scene. It could have a damage rating of a standard bow (strength) or based on something like composure instead and you may attack with a Athletics / Firearms + Dexterity again like a standard bow.<br /> <br /> If you want to draw on them gathering energy and their capacity does relate to their physical stamina possibly every 5 or so shots they need to make a check but this aspect I feel is not truly needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 05-26-2016, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:15:52-07:00","id":900522,"title":"","content":"Quincies died for me the moment &quot;Quincies only use bows and arrows&quot; did.<br /> <br /> (I know that isn't helpful in any way, but everything I conceived mechanically has already been suggested in some way. The only thought I have to add is that <i>Quincies should really use bows* </i>and beyond that solely accessories or tangential traits that round out their spiritual archery.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*I'm sorry but the Sternritter just have no thematic coherence.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-26-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T04:28:19-07:00","id":900823,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I woudl go with a Sin-Eater with a specific krewe mythos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T07:27:44-07:00","id":900938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/899766-closest-splat-to-a-bleach-quincy?p=900333#post900333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The problem is that this isn't true to Bleach canon.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Ishidas self-limited because they didn't want to get caught up in the Wandenreich and specifically Jhwach's plans.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The full abilities of the Quincy are highly varied.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> No, they absolutely aren't. The abilities of individual Quincies can vary, mostly by virtue of being given one of a kind special power ups from the first quincy, but the individual quincies only develop a handful of powers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Take Opie for example, he's shown about eight tricks up his sleeve, depending on such things as &quot;Do you count blut as one power or two?&quot; or &quot;Do you really consider making a sword out of spiritual energy and making arrows out of spiritual energy two powers or not?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> A mage character beats that number of tricks starting in character creation.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T10:06:50-07:00","id":901108,"title":"","content":"Ok...<br /> <br /> Quincy powers (that aren't the unique powers Jhwach grants is elites):<ul><li>Reishi Manipulation</li> <li>Spiritual Awareness</li> <li>Spirit Weapons - traditionally but not exclusively a bow, though all have ranged options.</li> <li>Mystic items - Quincy Cross, Hollow bait, Seele Schneider, Ginto, Sanrei Glove, Medalize, etc.</li> <li>Hirenkyaku</li> <li>Blut - as noted could be classified as more than one power since it has multiple applications</li> <li>Ransotengai</li> <li>Vollstandig</li> <li>Kirchenlied: Sankt Zwinger - which implies a whole set of powers we don't see since it establishes that Quincies have their own Kido like spells and is said to be the most powerful of its kind</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Can mages do more than that? Yes. But that's an extremely versatile list of powers, and isn't the totality of what they're capable of, that's just the standard stuff. Modelling that with Mage is going to be easier and faster than another other base splat at this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T16:18:41-07:00","id":901504,"title":"","content":"Could re-purposing Numina work, possibly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:39:59-07:00","id":901567,"title":"","content":"Numina and dread powers are generally meant for antagonists or npcs but if they can achieve what you want why not go with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}